help_replay
?
GG_replayhelp
Space: hide / show interface/rTab: hide / show the classification/rCtrl + Tab: hide / show the telemetry/rNumpad /: hide / show names/rRoll + Rotate Left, Right: roll Orbit / Free camera/rDouble Roll: reset Orbit / Free camera roll/rDecimal: cycle between Free camera modes/rNumpad 5: play/rNumpad 0: pause/rNumpad 7: rewind to the start/rNumpad 1: fast forward to the end/rNumpad 9: rewind/rNumpad 3: fast forward/rNumpad 4: rewind one frame/rNumpad 6: advance one frame/rNumpad 8: rewind slow-motion/rNumpad 2: slow-motion/rRight Alt + Subtract: previous camera/rRight Alt + Add: next camera/rRight Alt + Numpad 1 to Numpad 0: directly select camera from 1 to 10/rRight Shift + Subtract: previous rider on track/rRight Shift + Add: next rider on track/rRight Shift + Numpad 1 to Numpad 0: directly select rider from 1 to 10/r1 to 4 to switch camera / rider range to 11 - 50/r0 to go back to 1 - 10
viewer
Viewer
GG_lean
Click on this column to assign the controls
TT_cutstart
Set / remove Cut Start
TT_cutend
Set / remove Cut End
TT_live
Live feed
TT_rewindstart
Rewind to the start
TT_ffend
Fast forward to the end
TT_rewind
Rewind. Every successive press increases rewind rate
TT_rewindslow
Slow-motion rewind. Every successive press decreases rewind rate
TT_rewindframe
Rewind one frame
TT_playpause
Play / pause
TT_advanceframe
Advance one frame
TT_slowmotion
Slow-motion. Every successive press decreases advance rate
TT_fastforward
Fast forward. Every successive press increases advance rate
TT_savereplay
Save replay. The range can be limited using the "Cut Start" and "Cut End" buttons
TT_browser
D = dedicated server/rP = password protected/rComp = competitors/rCat = category/rH = hardcore mode. A: no aids; C: force cockpit; T: limited tyre sets; +: all/rW = weather. None: realistic; S: sunny; C: cloudy; R: rainy/rR = rating
TT_smooth
Smooths out the input adding a delay./rIt is useful for digital inputs and for gamepads
TT_linearity
100 means linear, direct, control./rMoving this slider toward non-linear gives more precision in the first part of the input, at the expense of the second part./rIt is useful for digital inputs and gamepads
TT_deadzone
Deadzone filters unwanted movements in the first part of the input./rIt is useful for analog inputs.
